## 6.1 Seed data to create

Every user-facing feature in this slice must include realistic seed data so the sandbox is demonstrable, not blank.

- Create or update Laravel seeder classes for this slice.
- Prefer multiple focused seeder classes so demo data is maintainable: users/roles, org/tenant structure, feature records, edge states, and relationship/linkage records.
- Seed at least 10 realistic records for each feature introduced or changed by this slice, unless the domain has fewer valid states.
- Seed every role/persona required to test this slice's flow and the full app journey, including admin, manager/approver, regular member, and restricted/read-only identities where the domain supports them.
- Include enough record states to make the UI obvious during review, such as draft, active, approved, rejected, overdue, archived, failed, or escalated where applicable.
- The first browser review after `php artisan migrate:fresh --seed` must show populated records, not empty states, on the primary app screens.
- Update `docs/user-manual/seed-data.md` with seeded records, credentials, reset commands, and removal/production notes.

## 6.2 Demo mode and user switcher

The sandbox `.env` must default to `DEMO_MODE=true`.

If this slice creates or modifies auth, navigation, layout, middleware, users, roles, permissions, tenancy, or any user-visible workflow, implement or preserve demo-mode behavior:

- When `DEMO_MODE=true`, reviewers must be able to access the app without logging in.
- When `DEMO_MODE=true`, the navbar must show a User Switcher populated from seeded demo users.
- The switcher must let reviewers impersonate/switch between seeded identities for the domain's major roles, departments/tenants, and permission levels.
- Switching users must change the effective current user for policies, queries, dashboards, and visible records.
- When `DEMO_MODE=false`, the User Switcher must be hidden and the app must require normal login by email/username and password.
- Production deployment must set `DEMO_MODE=false`.
- Document switcher identities and normal-login credentials in `docs/user-manual/seed-data.md`.

