## 12.1 Apply Laravel runtime changes and restart sandbox

After code changes, you are responsible for applying all required Laravel runtime commands. Do not ask the user to run migrations, seeders, cache clears, builds, queue restarts, or sandbox restarts for sandbox review.

Decide what is required from the files you changed:

- migrations/schema changes: `php artisan migrate --force`
- seeder/demo data changes: `php artisan db:seed --force`
- config/env/routes/events/views/container changes: `php artisan optimize:clear`
- frontend dependency changes: `npm install`
- frontend asset changes: `npm run build`
- queues/jobs/listeners/schedules: restart the queue worker, Horizon, scheduler, or the matching tmux process if present
- Octane/Reverb/Horizon/Vite/runtime config changes: restart the affected process
- route/controller/middleware/auth/layout changes: restart or reload the app server if the running sandbox will not pick them up automatically

Safe baseline when the slice changed app code:

```bash
php artisan optimize:clear
php artisan migrate --force
php artisan db:seed --force
npm run build
```

Then refresh the public sandbox from the current project root:

```bash
APP_PORT="$(awk -F: '/app_port:/ {gsub(/ /, "", $2); print $2}' docs/larv/STATE.yaml | tail -1)"
DB_DATABASE="$(awk -F: '/db_name:/ {gsub(/ /, "", $2); print $2}' docs/larv/STATE.yaml | tail -1)"

if [ -z "$APP_PORT" ] || [ "$APP_PORT" = "null" ]; then
  APP_PORT="$(grep -oE ':[0-9]+' docs/larv/07-runtime/sandbox-url.txt 2>/dev/null | tail -1 | tr -d ':')"
fi

if [ -z "$DB_DATABASE" ] || [ "$DB_DATABASE" = "null" ]; then
  DB_DATABASE="$(grep '^DB_DATABASE=' .env | cut -d= -f2-)"
fi

APP_PORT="$APP_PORT" DB_DATABASE="$DB_DATABASE" DEMO_MODE="${DEMO_MODE:-true}" bash docs/larv/07-runtime/deploy-sandbox.sh
```

Probe before announcing the URL:

```bash
SANDBOX_URL="$(cat docs/larv/07-runtime/sandbox-url.txt)"
curl -fsS --max-time 10 "$SANDBOX_URL" >/dev/null
printf "Sandbox ready: %s\n" "$SANDBOX_URL"
```

